      "status": "NOT CALLED -- classifier withdrawn after failing validation",
      "what_is_emitted": "per-segment nearest neighbours, k-mer distances, and normalized rank separations (sl_rank_separation, m_rank_offset) as continuous diagnostics only",
      "min_species_size": 8,
      "assessable_isolates": 1713,
      "why_withdrawn": "A classifier built on these rank separations produced the inverse of the reported literature ranking: ANDV 72% flagged (reported absent or sparse) vs PUUV 7.7% (reported 19.1-32%), and CHOV 100% at n=8. Sweeping the threshold from 0.25 to 0.85 scaled all rates down without changing the ordering. Cosine distance on 3-mer amino-acid composition tracks within-species diversity and sample size, not tree topology.",
      "to_detect_reassortment_properly": "Build per-segment alignments (MAFFT) and trees (IQ-TREE), then test topological incongruence between the S, M and L trees.",
      "trustworthy_signal": "taxonomic_incongruence -- NCBI assigning an isolate's segments to different species. This is metadata, not inference, and it does feed the risk score."
    },
